# Defect 2369, lane b26-cli, 2026-11-09: the module whose header defines
# `LIMIT` as a macro is walked first, so in the one file `--emit-c` writes the
# macro rewrites the other module's `enum` into C clang refuses. `build`
# prints 7 and 5. Until 2026-11-09 the one file was told in clang's words at
# the first module's group, and in the other order at the binding; both
# orders now name the binding the macro rewrites.
use aseven
use mlimit

function main()
    print(aseven.sevenfold())
    print(mlimit.limit())
